        "original_id": "b444515e-e224-57c4-9625-e4592dd65bb4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alan Campbell, William Conrad, Joe Penny\n- Roles: Derek Mitchell, E.Z. Taylor, J. L. \"Fatman\" McCabe, Jake Styles\n- TV series: Jake and the Fatman, Three's a Crowd\n- Topics: American television, film, and stage acting\n\nFacts:\n- Bruce Alan Campbell was born on April 22, 1957, and is professionally credited as Alan Campbell.\n- Alan Campbell is an American television, film, and stage actor.\n- Alan Campbell played E.Z. Taylor on the short-lived 1984–1985 Three's Company spin-off Three's a Crowd.\n- From 1987 to 1992, Alan Campbell played Derek Mitchell in the CBS series Jake and the Fatman.\n- Jake and the Fatman is a television crime drama.\n- William Conrad starred in Jake and the Fatman as prosecutor J. L. \"Jason Lochinvar\" McCabe, known as \"Fatman.\"\n- Joe Penny starred in Jake and the Fatman as investigator Jake Styles.",
